WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160 position:63% line:0%
Delegating a high-priority task to a person
who only delivers a bare-minimum style of

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.080 position:63% line:0%
work ethic otherwise, will probably result
in the task not getting done.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:14.240 position:63% line:0%
The Foundation tried to snuff out SCP-682
with the help of SCP-2599, formerly known

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:19.600 position:63% line:0%
as Zena Cho, a woman of Korean descent who’ll
carry out any order you give her...But only

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.880 position:63% line:0%
around halfway.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.160 position:63% line:0%
That’s why the Foundation ordered her to
attack 682 until it was “200% dead”, so

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.960 position:63% line:0%
even if she only did her task by halves, it’d
still be 100% dead.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.400 position:63% line:0%
By all accounts, she was actually doing a
pretty solid job, horrifically mutilating

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.200 position:63% line:0%
the creature to a point of near-death, when
it suddenly yelled “KILL ME, YOU SACK OF

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.320 position:63% line:0%
ORGANS, DO IT!”

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.480 position:63% line:0%
And that order seemingly confused her, seeing
as only going halfway on killing the creature

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.240 position:63% line:0%
was something she’d already done.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.840 position:63% line:0%
She remained motionless in the test chamber
until she was physically removed, and later

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.600 position:63% line:0%
attempts to use her in 682’s termination
were fruitless.

